<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Knighthood</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as knightly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Knighthood refers to the tradition of an elite class of mounted, heavily armed warriors bound by status and service to a ruler. Its armoured cavalry influenced Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a> and, through several channels of transmission, the medieval European knightly tradition. Elite horsemen of this kind were the backbone of Sasanian military power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/knighthood.jpg" alt="Knighthood" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meister des Codex Manesse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
